+# Glossary
+
+- **On-hand** — physical units of a SKU in a warehouse, derived from the ledger.
+- **Allocated** — units promised to PLACED orders that have not shipped yet.
+- **Held** — units held by ACTIVE (not lapsed) reservations.
+- **Available** — on-hand − allocated − held, per SKU per warehouse, floored at 0.
+- **Reservation / hold** — a time-limited claim on available stock for a cart,
+  made before payment. Ends CONFIRMED (became an order), RELEASED (given back)
+  or EXPIRED (lapsed). See `specs/stock-reservations.md`.
+- **Partial hold** — a reservation holding fewer units than requested on some
+  line, because only that much was available (ADR 0003).
+- **TTL** — how long a reservation holds stock; `expires_at` = creation + TTL
+  (default 20 minutes).
+- **Lapsed** — an ACTIVE reservation whose `expires_at` is at or before now;
+  treated as EXPIRED from that instant (ADR 0001).
+- **Idempotency key** — caller-chosen key on `reserve` making retries safe;
+  bound to warehouse + requested items (ADR 0002).
