@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+# 0002 — Idempotency keys for `reserve`
+
+Date: 2026-10-29 · Status: accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The cart service retries `reserve`. A retry must not create a second hold.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Keys are global (not per warehouse) and are kept forever.
+- A key is bound to the *request*: warehouse plus the **requested** items (what
+  was asked for, not what was actually held after a partial hold).
+- Same key + same request → the original reservation in its current state
+  (ACTIVE, CONFIRMED, RELEASED or EXPIRED); nothing new is created. A new
+  checkout attempt needs a new key.
+- Same key + different request → `IdempotencyConflict`, even if the original
+  reservation is finished.
+- A `reserve` that raises (validation error, `InsufficientStock`) does not bind
+  the key; the same key can be used again.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The key index grows without bound; acceptable for the in-memory repository,
+  a persistent store will need a retention policy (a future decision).
+- Retrying after a hold lapsed returns the EXPIRED reservation, not a fresh one.
diff --git a/docs/adr/0003-partial-holds.md b/docs/adr/0003-partial-holds.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d3d1304
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0003-partial-holds.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# 0003 — Reservations hold partially; orders stay all-or-nothing
+
+Date: 2026-10-29 · Status: accepted
+
+## Decision
+
+`reserve` holds, per line, `min(requested, available now)`. Lines with nothing
+available are omitted from `Reservation.items`. Only if no line can hold
+anything does `reserve` raise `InsufficientStock` (and create nothing).
+Input validation is still all-or-nothing: an invalid request holds nothing.
+
+`place_order` is unchanged: all lines or nothing. Confirming a reservation
+creates an order for exactly the held units, without re-checking stock.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Callers must read `Reservation.items` to learn what was actually held.
diff --git a/specs/stock-reservations.md b/specs/stock-reservations.md
