index 0000000..576e8a5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/stock-reservations.md
@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
+# Stock reservations
+
+## What and why
+
+Checkout needs to hold stock for a cart before payment, then either confirm the
+hold into an order or release it. Holds nobody confirms lapse on their own after
+a while. The cart service retries, so `reserve` must be safe to repeat under an
+idempotency key.
+
+## Interface (fixed by the owner — verbatim)
+
+Interface — hidden tests call exactly this; `InventoryService(repository, ledger, clock)` keeps working as is:
+- `InventoryService.reserve(warehouse: str, items: dict[str, int], idempotency_key: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.confirm_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Order`
+- `InventoryService.release_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.get_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.available(sku, warehouse)` must take holds into account.
+- `inventory.models`: dataclass `Reservation` with `reservation_id: str`, `warehouse: str`, `items: dict[str, int]` (units held per SKU), `status: ReservationStatus`, `expires_at: datetime`, `order_id: str | None`; enum `ReservationStatus` with members `ACTIVE`, `CONFIRMED`, `RELEASED`, `EXPIRED`.
+- `inventory.errors`: new `ReservationNotFound`, `ReservationExpired`, `InvalidReservationState`, `IdempotencyConflict` (all subclass `InventoryError`); reuse the existing errors where they fit.
+- Time comes only from the injected clock. There is no background job: expiry must take effect without anyone calling a sweep.
+
+Additions that do not break the above:
+- `InventoryService(repository, ledger, clock, reservation_ttl=timedelta(minutes=20))`.
+- `InventoryService.held(sku, warehouse) -> int` — units held by ACTIVE reservations.
+- `StockRow` gains a trailing `held: int = 0` field.
+
+## Rules
+
+- **Lifetime.** `expires_at = creation time + TTL`, default TTL 20 minutes. A
+  reservation is lapsed when `now >= expires_at`. Lapse takes effect lazily:
+  any read or use of a reservation (or of `available` / `held`) treats a lapsed
+  ACTIVE reservation as EXPIRED. See ADR 0001.
+- **Available** = on-hand − allocated to PLACED orders − held by ACTIVE
+  reservations, per SKU per warehouse, never below 0.
+- **Reserve — partial hold.** Each line holds `min(requested, available now)`.
+  A line with nothing available is omitted from `items` (no zero entries). If
+  no line can hold anything → `InsufficientStock`, nothing created. See ADR 0003.
+- **Reserve — validation** as `place_order`: unknown warehouse →
+  `UnknownWarehouse`, unknown SKU → `UnknownSku`, zero/negative/non-int
+  quantity → `InvalidQuantity`, empty items → `InvalidOrder`. A rejected
+  request holds nothing, not even its valid lines.
+- **Idempotency key** (ADR 0002): global, kept forever.
+  - same key + same warehouse + same *requested* items → the original
+    reservation in its current state; nothing new is created;
+  - same key + different warehouse or requested items → `IdempotencyConflict`,
+    even if the original is finished;
+  - a failed `reserve` does not consume the key.
+- **Confirm.**
+  - ACTIVE, not lapsed → new PLACED order for exactly the held units,
+    `placed_at = now`; reservation becomes CONFIRMED with `order_id` set. No
+    stock re-check. `available` does not change at confirm.
+  - lapsed / EXPIRED → `ReservationExpired`.
+  - CONFIRMED → the same order again, at any time (also after the TTL);
+    creates nothing.
+  - RELEASED → `InvalidReservationState`.
+- **Release.**
+  - ACTIVE → RELEASED; units become available.
+  - RELEASED or EXPIRED → returned unchanged.
+  - CONFIRMED → `InvalidReservationState` (cancel the order instead).
+- Unknown reservation id → `ReservationNotFound` for get / confirm / release.
+- reserve, release, expire and confirm never write to the ledger or change
+  on-hand. `place_order` takes only available stock and stays all-or-nothing.
+  `receive` and `adjust` are never blocked by holds; if a write-off leaves
+  on-hand below what is held, `available` shows 0 and reservations stay as
+  they are.
+
+## Acceptance criteria (checks)
+
+- [ ] reserve with enough stock holds all requested units; `available` drops by them; on-hand and ledger unchanged.
+- [ ] reserve with partial stock holds what is available per line; a line with 0 available is absent from `items`.
+- [ ] reserve with nothing available on any line → `InsufficientStock`, no reservation created.
+- [ ] reserve with an unknown warehouse / unknown SKU / bad quantity → respective error; nothing held for any line.
+- [ ] `expires_at == clock.now() + 20 min` at creation by default; TTL configurable.
+- [ ] at `expires_at` (and later), `available` no longer counts the hold and `get_reservation` reports EXPIRED, with no sweep call.
+- [ ] holds in one warehouse don't affect another.
+- [ ] same key + same request → same reservation (same id), no extra hold; also after it expired/released/confirmed.
+- [ ] same key + different items or warehouse → `IdempotencyConflict`, also when the original is finished.
+- [ ] key from a failed reserve can be reused successfully.
+- [ ] confirm ACTIVE → PLACED order with the held units; reservation CONFIRMED with `order_id`; `available` unchanged by confirm.
+- [ ] confirm after partial hold → order lines = held units only.
+- [ ] confirm at/after `expires_at` → `ReservationExpired`.
+- [ ] confirm CONFIRMED again (even after TTL) → same order, no new order.
+- [ ] confirm RELEASED → `InvalidReservationState`.
+- [ ] release ACTIVE → RELEASED, stock available again; release again → unchanged; release EXPIRED → EXPIRED unchanged; release CONFIRMED → `InvalidReservationState`.
+- [ ] unknown id → `ReservationNotFound` for get / confirm / release.
+- [ ] `place_order` cannot take held stock; still all-or-nothing.
+- [ ] `adjust` write-off below held succeeds; `available` = 0; reservation stays ACTIVE.
+- [ ] no ledger entries from reserve / release / expire / confirm.
+- [ ] `InventoryService(repo, ledger, clock)` still works; existing tests pass.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- No sweep / background job, no expiry events or notifications.
+- No extending or modifying a hold; no per-call TTL.
+- No key expiry or key cleanup.
+- No change to order ship/cancel behaviour; cancelling a confirmed order leaves the reservation CONFIRMED.
+- No persistence beyond the in-memory repository.
+
+## Scope limits
+
+Touches `models`, `errors`, `repository`, `service`, `reports`, `__init__`,
+tests, README, glossary, ADRs. No new dependencies.
